{
  "about": "The static status glyphs (Leo 2026-10-14, the Static status mode for Reduce Motion): one shape per state, no animation, tinted by a theme role. gen-status-glyphs.py writes the Swift and web copies. Coordinates run y-down. `master` sits on a 20-unit grid (10 pt at 2x: one unit is one pixel), `x1art` is the 10 px (1x) drawing as pixel art (# is ink), so every edge falls on a pixel. Ops: [M x y], [L x y], [C x1 y1 x2 y2 x y], [arc cx cy r fromDeg toDeg] (continues the path, degrees grow clockwise on screen), [circle cx cy r], [Z]. Every glyph fills even-odd, so an inner shape cuts out. A glyph's `set` says which set draws it (static unless named). `sets` maps each state of another set to a glyph and a tint: the Codex-like set (Leo's team, 2026-10-14) draws Codex's thin line symbols, a neutral spinner (the app's own spinner, re-tinted) and Codex's blue dot. The Dots and Pictograms sets (hq#1957 status glyph thunderdome, behind the Debug status icon switch) draw the same states with the static set's tints.",
